.faq", "pk": 1, "fields": {"question": "Is it working ?", "answer": "Hell Yeah", "created_at": "2025-10-24T16:08:51.742Z", "updated_at": "2025-10-24T16:08:51.742Z"}}, {"model": "banner.faq", "pk": 2, "fields": {"question": "What types of fabrics are best for hijab outfits?", "answer": "Lightweight and breathable fabrics such as cotton, chiffon, and jersey are ideal for hijab outfits, as they provide comfort and ease of styling.", "created_at": "2025-10-24T16:12:43.867Z", "updated_at": "2025-10-24T16:12:43.867Z"}}, {"model": "banner.faq", "pk": 3, "fields": {"question": "How do I choose the right color for my hijab?", "answer": "Choose a color that complements your skin tone and outfit. Neutral colors like beige, white, and black work for everyday wear, while bright colors are perfect for special occasions.", "created_at": "2025-10-24T16:13:27.737Z", "updated_at": "2025-10-24T16:13:27.737Z"}}, {"model": "banner.faq", "pk": 4, "fields": {"question": "Are there hijab styles suitable for formal events?", "answer": "Yes, you can opt for silk or satin hijabs for formal occasions. They give a more elegant and polished look, especially when paired with dresses or abayas.", "created_at": "2025-10-24T16:13:58.752Z", "updated_at": "2025-10-24T16:13:58.752Z"}}, {"model": "banner.faq", "pk": 5, "fields": {"question": "How can I keep my hijab in place all day?", "answer": "Use undercaps, magnetic pins, or small safety pins to secure your hijab. Choosing a non-slippery fabric also helps keep it in place.", "created_at": "2025-10-24T16:14:23.225Z", "updated_at": "2025-10-24T16:14:23.225Z"}}, {"model": "banner.faq", "pk": 6, "fields": {"question": "How should I wash and care for my hijabs?", "answer": "Hand wash or use a gentle cycle in cold water. Avoid wringing or tumble drying to keep the fabric smooth and prevent damage.", "created_at": "2025-10-24T16:14:56.033Z", "updated_at": "2025-10-24T16:14:56.033Z"}}, {"model": "orders.order", "pk": 1, "fields": {"public_id": "245f4522-e9e